1)\tab\tab Well-written programs include internal safeguards to prevent \tab\tab scenarios that violate obscure nuanced details of the \tab\tab\tab\tab program such as requiring a particular symbol to be \tab\tab\tab\tab maintained within a narrow address range [or at a particular \tab\tab location in memory].  Analysis of the error message report \tab\tab\tab may help the maintenance programmer determine what \tab\tab\tab\tab programming blunder was committed.\par
