P?S/8 PAL Directives.\par
\par
ASMIFM \i expression\i0\par
\par
\tab\tab The ASMIFM directive is one of the conditional assembly \tab\tab\tab features of the extended PAL language.  See Note 1.\par
\par
\tab\tab The specified \i expression\i0  is evaluated.  If the result is \tab\tab\tab negative, the next line is assembled.  If the result is \tab\tab\tab positive, the next line is ignored.\par
\par
\tab\tab ASMIFM\tab A-B\tab\tab\tab /COMPARE A TO B.\par
\tab\tab D=3\tab\tab\tab\tab\tab /SET D TO 0003.\par
\par
\tab\tab The next line may be blank or consist of comments only \tab\tab\tab rendering the conditional moot.  During the early \tab\tab\tab\tab development of a program, this may deliberately be done to \tab\tab\tab force a specific outcome.\par
\par
\tab\tab Note: If additional statements are on the same line as the \tab\tab\tab ASMIFM directive [using \highlight1 ;\highlight0  to separate the statements] and \tab\tab\tab the conditional test fails, the additional statements are \tab\tab\tab also ignored.\par
\par
