ASMSKP \i expression\i0\par
\par
\tab\tab The ASMSKP directive is one of the conditional assembly \tab\tab\tab features of the extended PAL language.  See Note 1.\par
\par
\tab\tab The specified \i expression\i0  is evaluated as an unsigned 12-bit \tab\tab integer value.  The next \i expression\i0  value lines of the \tab\tab\tab source code are ignored.\par
\par
\tab\tab ASMSKP\tab 3\tab\tab\tab /SKIP THE NEXT THREE LINES.\par
\tab\tab HLT\tab\tab\tab\tab\tab /THIS IS IGNORED!\par
\tab\tab JMP\tab\tab .+3\tab\tab\tab /THIS IS ALSO IGNORED!\par
\tab\tab /\tab\tab\tab\tab\tab IGNORED AND ALSO A COMMENT!\par
\par
\tab\tab If the \i expression\i0  evaluates to zero, all lines following the \tab\tab ASMSKP directive will be assembled.  If the \i expression\i0  \tab\tab\tab evaluates to a non-zero value and additional statments are \tab\tab\tab on the same line as the ASMSKP directive [using \highlight1 ;\highlight0  to \tab\tab\tab\tab separate the statements], the additional statements are also \tab\tab ignored.\par
\par
\tab\tab Note: The need for the ASMSKP directive comes about because \tab\tab of the complex nature of conditional assembly using the \tab\tab\tab provided directives [certain logical expressions might \tab\tab\tab require the use of multiple conditionals].  Unfortunely, \tab\tab\tab since the ASMSKP directive does not work with any form of\tab\tab\tab delimiter mechanism, the programmer must carefully count the \tab\tab lines expected to be skipped; changes to the program source \tab\tab can cause unexpected results.\page\cf3 Appendix B [continued].\cf1\f1\par
