\tab\tab The \i statements\i0  can span an indefinite number of lines of \tab\tab\tab source code as necessary.  Conditionals are occasionally \tab\tab\tab used within other conditionals in a "nested" manner.  The \tab\tab\tab count of  \highlight1 <\highlight0  and \highlight1 >\highlight0  must be carefully maintained to achieve an \tab\tab error-free assembly.\par
\par
\tab\tab Note: The contents of comments are scanned for \highlight1 <\highlight0  and \highlight1 >\highlight0  when \tab\tab conditional assembly is in effect.\page\cf3 Appendix B [continued].\cf1\f1\par
\cf0\f2\par
\tab\tab The IFNDEF directive is often used to initialize a symbol \tab\tab\tab default value:\par
